## Core guarantees

- Deterministic output (same inputs -> same bytes)
- No code execution in templates
- Schema validation happens before rendering
- Safe recursion: cycle detection + depth/size limits
- Fail fast on the first error

## When it fits

Use arb when:
- one source of truth must drive many outputs
- consistency matters more than convenience
- you want deterministic rebuilds

Avoid arb when:
- you need runtime side effects or arbitrary computation in templates
